{"base_rate":0.349002849002849,"brier":0.16517193732193733,"bss":0.273010392533381,"bss_hi":0.34622280331213906,"bss_lo":0.18506720532194787,"chart":{"base":[363.7,170.9],"fp":[415.2,327.2],"lead":"62,284.1 272,259.8 482,210.7 692,138.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 44% of cities","fp":"low end +13pp, high end +2pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 95% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 12%; promised 83% → rained 81%"},"rel":"62,415 107.2,368.6 279.9,272 582.4,116.1"},"country":"DZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.10149572649572651,"ess":330.3610946570303,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Constantine</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Constantine rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (94%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>12%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 702 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 9.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 121 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(78&ndash;154) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>271</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>37%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>54%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Constantine</b> <span class=\"muted\">Algeria</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;35% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 35% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>78&ndash;154\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>702 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Constantine &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Constantine\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.013062730627304,382.0 71.60105263157894,348.4736842105263 96.99363636363637,310.3030303030303 149.08692307692309,251.33333333333334 215.91478260869565,176.2608695652174 306.6208695652174,91.85507246376812 391.8268493150685,22.986301369863043 391.8268493150685,57.89041095890411 306.6208695652174,165.71014492753625 215.91478260869565,260.6666666666667 149.08692307692309,321.3333333333333 96.99363636363637,365.45454545454544 71.60105263157894,382.0 58.013062730627304,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"254.96296296296296\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"254.96296296296296\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.013062730627304,339.01845018450183 71.60105263157894,314.9473684210526 96.99363636363637,282.72727272727275 149.08692307692309,246.66666666666666 215.91478260869565,186.81159420289853 306.6208695652174,128.7826086956522 391.8268493150685,47.917808219178085\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 271 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.013062730627304\" cy=\"339.01845018450183\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"71.60105263157894\" cy=\"314.9473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"96.99363636363637\" cy=\"282.72727272727275\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 26%&amp;#10;It rained 37% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"149.08692307692309\" cy=\"246.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 54% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"215.91478260869565\" cy=\"186.81159420289853\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 70% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"306.6208695652174\" cy=\"128.7826086956522\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 92% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"391.8268493150685\" cy=\"47.917808219178085\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(35%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Constantine the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.41) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.065</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>148</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.198</td><td class='num'>18.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.222</td><td class='num'>12.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'>0.406</td><td class='num'>1.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":36.365,"lon":6.61472,"n":702,"n_cities":216,"name":"Constantine","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":3.690036900369004e-05,"n":271,"obs":0.11808118081180811,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03842105263157893,"n":76,"obs":0.18421052631578946,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.11015151515151514,"n":66,"obs":0.2727272727272727,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3440000000000009,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.2573076923076923,"n":78,"obs":0.3717948717948718,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6,"lo":0.3440000000000009,"mean":0.44608695652173913,"n":69,"obs":0.5362318840579711,"sig":false},{"hi":0.83,"lo":0.6,"mean":0.7023188405797102,"n":69,"obs":0.6956521739130435,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.83,"mean":0.9430136986301371,"n":73,"obs":0.9178082191780822,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":9.9,"provisional":false,"rank":121,"rank_hi":154.02499999999998,"rank_lo":78.0,"reliability":0.012490795569129014,"resolution":0.07303137333724447,"skill_pc